# /enrich-entities

Generalizes Topwater's `/enrich-companies`. Pulls deeper, usually-paid data
on only the {{vocabulary.entityPlural}} scoring already qualified — never
on everything discovered.

---

## Before anything

Load `standards/OUTPUT-STANDARDS.md` Rule O4. Unit of reuse: the
{{vocabulary.entity}}. A qualifying {{vocabulary.entity}} with no
enrichment row yet, or one whose tier just changed into scope, is new work;
one already enriched is not redone.

## Eligibility — the spend gate

Only {{vocabulary.entityPlural}} in a qualifying tier
(`{{budget.enrichmentEligibleTiers|| "the tiers marked eligible in criteria.tiers"}}`)
are eligible for this step. Never enrich a {{vocabulary.entity}} that
scoring already marked as an outright pass or as an ineligible tier — this
is the deliberate reason scoring runs as its own separate stage before this
one: paying an `enrichment` connector for a {{vocabulary.entity}} that
scoring already ruled out wastes real budget for no possible benefit.

---

## What this skill does

1. For each eligible {{vocabulary.entity}}, calls the configured
   `enrichment` connector(s) ({{connectors.enrichment}}) per that
   connector's own `prompt-fragment.md` (field limits, rate limits).
2. Never guesses a field the connector didn't return — missing enrichment
   data follows `criteria.onMissingData` the same as missing discovery
   data: null and flagged, never invented.
3. Logs every paid call (connector, {{vocabulary.entity}} count, and
   whatever credit/cost unit that connector reports) to a usage ledger —
   generalizes Topwater's CLAUDE.md Section 6 "log every run" discipline
   and the `budget` block's advisory role in
   `docs/CONFIG-SCHEMA.md`.

---

## Output format

```json
{
  "{{pipeline.stageA.unitNoun|| "category"}}": "",
  "enriched_at": "",
  "{{vocabulary.entityPlural}}": [
    { "name": "", "tier": "", "enrichment": {}, "missing_fields": [] }
  ]
}
```

Save per `standards/OUTPUT-STANDARDS.md` Rule O1; produce and PDF a
readable summary per Rule O2.
